@!internal

--- The readiness system calls under the native core's reactor, as its host
--- answers them: kqueue on macOS and epoll on Linux, behind one shape. A call
--- of one is the core's own library call, and requiring this module loads
--- nothing: it exists only on the core, for `nupp.runtime.reactor`. Each
--- answers what the system call did, or the negated error number.
local record pollcalls
    --- A new poller's descriptor.
    open: function(): integer

    --- Sets the readiness `poller` waits for on `descriptor` to `interest`:
    --- 1 readable and 2 writable, added together, or 0 for none. Interest
    --- lasts for one event; after it the descriptor is armed again. 0 when
    --- it is set.
    arm: function(poller: integer, descriptor: integer, interest: integer): integer

    --- Waits at most `nanos` nanoseconds, or without limit when it is -1, for
    --- one event: its descriptor times 32, plus 1 readable, 2 writable, 4
    --- hung up and 8 failed; or a child's process id times 32 plus 16, for
    --- its exit (`processcalls.watch`); 0 when the time passed first or a
    --- signal interrupted the wait.
    wait: function(poller: integer, nanos: integer): integer

    --- A pipe whose ends are nonblocking and close on exec: the read end's
    --- descriptor plus the write end's times 2^32.
    pipe: function(): integer
end

local calls: pollcalls
return calls
